      "location": "A Sabana Occidente municipality west of Bogotá, on the Cundinamarca savanna.",
      "history": "The settlement known as Cuatro Esquinas became a municipality in 1861 and was named Mosquera in honor of Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera. The area also records Muisca and paleontological remains."
